## 2.4 Trading execution safety

IMPORTANT:

Do not expose unrestricted live order-placement tools to Gemini or MCP.

MCP must not bypass the existing risk-management engine.

Do not implement unrestricted tools such as:
- Execute any live BUY order.
- Execute any live SELL order.
- Modify arbitrary broker positions.
- Disable risk restrictions.
- Disable the kill switch.

If a paper-trading action tool is useful, it must:

1. Work only with the simulated paper account.
2. Validate all arguments.
3. Pass through the existing risk engine.
4. Require explicit user confirmation through the application UI.
5. Record an audit event.
6. Return the actual simulated execution status.

All future live broker actions must require a separate controlled workflow with applicable regulatory and broker checks.

MCP tools must never have permission to alter their own access restrictions.

